---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { url } from '../lib/paths';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Terms & Conditions | Best OutDoor Wears"
  description="Terms and conditions for using bestoutdoorwears.com and purchasing TrailReady."
  canonicalPath="/terms/"
>
  <section>
    <div class="wrap prose legal-page" style="max-width:74ch; padding-top:20px;">
      <h1>Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
      <p class="mono" style="font-size:0.8rem;">Last updated: August 24, 2026</p>

      <h2>Using this site</h2>
      <p>
        By using bestoutdoorwears.com, you agree to use it for lawful purposes and not to copy, resell, or
        redistribute our content or the TrailReady product without permission.
      </p>

      <h2>Content is informational, not professional advice</h2>
      <p>
        Guides on this site describe general outdoor clothing and layering principles. They are not a substitute
        for checking your own local forecast, trail conditions, and personal risk tolerance before any trip.
        Outdoor activities carry inherent risk; use your own judgment.
      </p>

      <h2>Purchases</h2>
      <p>
        TrailReady is a digital product delivered instantly after purchase through our payment provider (Payhip
        or Gumroad). Because it's a digital download available immediately, purchases are generally final —
        see our refund approach below.
      </p>

      <h2>Refunds</h2>
      <p>
        If TrailReady doesn't download correctly or isn't as described, contact us within 14 days of purchase
        and we'll make it right. We don't offer refunds simply for a change of mind once the files have been
        downloaded, in line with standard digital-goods practice.
      </p>

      <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
      <p>
        Some links on this site are affiliate links; see our <a href={url('/affiliate-disclosure/')}>affiliate
        disclosure</a> for details.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        We provide this site and TrailReady "as is." We aren't liable for outcomes of your outdoor trips —
        that responsibility rests with you and your own preparation and judgment.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>We may update these terms; the date above reflects the latest revision.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about these terms? Reach us via our <a href={url('/contact/')}>contact page</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
